t":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Cliques","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/enumerated()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enumerated"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"enumerated()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/enumerated()","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/enumerated()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"}}}